From b29039819af273ce451044c03e4ececb1efd8242 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Jhong <dylan@andestech.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Apr 2023 11:46:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 015/241] target/riscv: Introduce new Andes CSR read/write
 operations with "write any, read any" approach

The current operation of Andes CSRs is "write any, read zero". However,
in our software, there are cases where we write values to these CSRs
and then read the written values to confirm if the settings are successful,
for example, $mcache_ctl, $pmaaddr, etc. Therefore, we need to change the
previous "write any, read zero" strategy.

The new strategy is "write any, read any". The software will be able to
set values for all Andes CSRs and expect to read back the same values.
This approach should resolve most software issues. However, if the software
checks the default values of certain Andes CSRs, it may read back values
of 0, which could potentially result in incorrect judgments. However,
this can be corrected when encountering actual issues in the future.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Jhong <dylan@andestech.com>
